Clarification 1: Mark-up Ownership / Authorization

Subject: Clarification on Mark-up Record Authorization

During testing, we observed that users are able to create Mark-up records on the map. We would like to confirm the intended authorization model for this functionality.

Specifically:

Should a user who creates a Mark-up record (User A) be the only user permitted to modify or delete that record?
Or is it expected that other authorized users (User B) can also modify or delete Mark-up records created by different users?
If shared modification/deletion is intended, are there any role-based restrictions (e.g., Administrators, Supervisors, Editors) that govern this behavior?

Reason for clarification

This information will help us determine whether the observed behavior is intended business functionality or represents a potential authorization (Broken Access Control/IDOR) issue.

